    "blocks": [
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Asciidoctor’s HTML5 converter has a built-in method for generating an HTML TOC. This TOC generator can also be used as a general purpose API. This logic is available via the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "convert_outline"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " method (which is the convert method for the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "outline"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " node) on the HTML5 converter."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          }
        ],
        "context": "preamble",
        "id": null,
        "outline": null,
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "The "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "convert_outline"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " method accepts a Document object and an optional Hash of options and it returns HTML. It can be resolved and invoked as a general purpose method using the following snippet of code:"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "listing",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "document = Asciidoctor.load_file 'document-with-sections.adoc', safe: :safe\nhtml_toc = (Asciidoctor::Converter.create 'html5').convert_outline document\nputs html_toc"
              }
            ],
            "language": "ruby",
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Here’s an example of what this method produces:"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "listing",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "<ul class=\"sectlevel1\">\n<li><a href=\"#_section_a\">Section A</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#_section_b\">Section B</a>\n<ul class=\"sectlevel2\">\n<li><a href=\"#_subsection\">Subsection</a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li><a href=\"#_section_c\">Section C</a></li>\n</ul>"
              }
            ],
            "language": "html",
            "roles": [
              "output"
            ],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "You can also access the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "convert_outline"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " method on the converter instance by way of the Document API:"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "listing",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "document = Asciidoctor.load_file 'document-with-sections.adoc', safe: :safe\nhtml_toc = document.converter.convert_outline document"
              }
            ],
            "language": "ruby",
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "If you’re using a composite converter, you can use the generic "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "convert"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " method to ensure the call is run through the converter chain. To do so, invoke the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "convert"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " method and pass in the Document object and the node name "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "outline"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ". This, in turn, will call "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "convert_outline"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " on the converter in the chain that responds to this method."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "listing",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "document = Asciidoctor.load_file 'document-with-sections.adoc', safe: :safe\nhtml_doc = document.converter.convert document, 'outline'"
              }
            ],
            "language": "ruby",
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "You can also use this method inside any converter template (e.g., Slim, Haml, or ERB) to generate and embed a TOC:"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "listing",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "= converter.convert document, 'outline'"
              }
            ],
            "language": "ruby",
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          }
        ],
        "context": "section",
        "id": "_usage",
        "level": 1,
        "roles": [],
